{"kind":"assert","text":"Review note for Hugh: make contract evidence independent and label what was rerun.\n\nTwo reviewed tasks expose the same gap. In #20424, [the store fixture](internal/gitstore/preview_test.go@72cb466f719fe4ae91e9bd91da1451bfb198fbfa:32) and [HTTP fixture](internal/service/preview_test.go@72cb466f719fe4ae91e9bd91da1451bfb198fbfa:220) construct the oversized input from the production limit. Raising that limit grows the fixtures too. The independent R3 review #20783 (74c50b7a) demonstrated that changing 4 MiB to 8 MiB still passes the committed preview tests; fixed 4194304/4194305-byte controls detect it. The current source enforces 4 MiB: this is a missing regression proof, not a production over-limit read. Earlier, #3722 (b42b5a9d) records why the citation baseline needed another round: implementation mutations missed a bad citation spreading to another page because the comparison omitted the page set. The test data, not just the code, needed to vary.\n\nMy recommendation is a small authoring habit before requesting review: for a numerical limit, allowed set or scope boundary, name one expected result independently of the production value, and one realistic way the implementation or input could violate it. Show the passing control and the failing violation on the candidate being offered. A test derived from the same constant or enumeration can still check internal consistency; it cannot alone pin the external contract. This belongs in focused tests and concise evidence, not a new checklist ceremony.\n\nAlso keep current and carried-forward proof distinct. The #20765 artifact describes twelve Go mutations caught across several heads, while #20753 says a raised-cap mutation fails at this exact head; the reviewer found otherwise. A compact evidence attachment should identify the condition, fixture/expected result, mutation, tested head and outcome. If evidence was inherited, say so and check that both the tested implementation and fixture still justify it. Do not present a historical total as current-head coverage. Keep the primary artifact short and link that attachment.\n\nExpected benefit: reviewers can target the remaining uncertainty, and authors catch moving-oracle tests before another review round. This is a recommendation for your review, not a new state transition, implementation assignment, or permission to skip required exact-head checks and final gates. The present preview correction remains on its existing promise; no additional task is needed to finish it.","body":{"head":"72cb466f719fe4ae91e9bd91da1451bfb198fbfa","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:74c50b7a01fce3ea6bdccf6eb36175ed328ffb15, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b42b5a9d2bd4e6635f20767b3bc65b5b70921dc3, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b879500eba3e328811faff6e92fe60b2a5fa3d3d stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0289268d00f17d2f7a127faead22bc78ee18dd4c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02ce62ac39d438188a2ab6ac783b4edf22d7bd5e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f and 143 more"}}